rectly with you  and trust that it's real and you know  what I'm excited to go see the concert  the blockchain is open transparent and  mutable anyone can go to a website and  see the transactions happen whereby it's  incredibly hard to change a transaction  once it has occurred transparency  creates trust trusts forms the basis of  community the real human truth about  blockchain this is not just about  changing the way we transact money it's  about leveraging the technology shared  record of truth to establish trust  between people companies or even nations  and exchange what we value which is the  whole point of a community the human  experience is tribal and live  experiences cannot be digitally  replicated when the music hits you  that's something very real and visceral  and non digital it is just an incredible  feeling  [Music]  music is inextricably a part of who I am  because when it all comes crumbling down  we'll still have song and dance around  the fire and we're still gonna tell  stories it's part of the human  experience and without it we'd just be a  bunch of ones and zeros  [Music]
 

